<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lydia</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Lydian kingdom</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lydia was a kingdom in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a> with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sardis">Sardis</a>, famous for its wealth and for early coinage. Its last king, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croesus">Croesus</a>, was defeated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyrus-the-great">Cyrus the Great</a> around 547 BCE. The conquest brought Lydia and the Greek cities of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ionia">Ionia</a> into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaemenid-empire">Achaemenid Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lydia.jpg" alt="Lydia" width="320" height="179" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ennomus · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kingdom_of_Lydia.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
